Henchmen are a great idea, perhaps you could meet them in the dungeon, and
pay them with gold.  And they could fight with you, or not, and they could
scarf up all gold they see for themselves.  They could also pick up magic
items for themselves.  So, they could be a pain as well as a boon.  They
could also use magic items and weapons.  Perhaps they could have classes
and alignments.  A chaotic henchman may attack you, or run off with your
possesions when you're unconcious.  A lawful henchman may give you things
to help you or guard you when you're unconcious.  Alignments wouldn't be
obvious at first.

Potential henchman would could also have their own (perhaps powerful) magic
items.  They could be fierce opponents (if angered).  And they could give
rogues an opportunity to do their stuff: rob people.  Rogues should be
able to pick pockets of other humanoids (or those that have pockets).  
Currently the Rogue is the weakest character.  This ability could even
him up with other characters.  Potential henchman of course could be a
source of magic items for the Rogue.

